concepts.body_md:
**Prompt** us conversation ke andar ek instruction hai jisme tum pehle se ho. Woh sab kuch usi conversation se udhaar leta hai: uski history, uske tools, uska permission mode, aur jawab check karne ke liye tumhara dhyan. **Template** ek prompt hai jo tumne save kar liya taaki dobara paste kar sako. Claude Code mein template ka saved, versioned form **skill** hai (`.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`): wahi idea, plus supporting files, arguments (`$ARGUMENTS`, pehle wale ke liye `$0`) aur ek optional `/name` entry point.

**Agent** (Claude Code subagent, `.claude/agents/<name>.md`) kind mein alag hai, wording mein nahi. `build/CLAUDE_CODE_FACTS.md` §1 ke hisaab se uske paas hai:

- **apni context window**: woh apni file body ko system prompt ke roop mein, task message, CLAUDE.md hierarchy, git status aur koi bhi preloaded `skills` ke saath start hota hai. Use tumhari conversation history, Claude Code system prompt, tumhara output style ya auto memory **nahi** milti;
- **apni tool boundary**: `tools` ek allowlist hai, `disallowedTools` ek denylist;
- **apni authority**: `permissionMode`, `maxTurns`, `model`, optional `memory`, `hooks` aur `isolation: worktree`;
- **ek loop**: woh tools call karta rehta hai jab tak use lage ki kaam ho gaya, phir main session ko **ek final message** return karta hai.

Isliye practical test yeh nahi hai ki "prompt lamba hai kya". Test yeh hai: *kya is kaam ko us conversation se alag context, alag tools, ya alag authority chahiye jo ise maang rahi hai?* Bench par jawab aksar haan hota hai. Jis session ne abhi `sl_patient.json` mein naya field likha, woh us JSON ka independent reviewer nahi hai. Jis reviewer ke paas `Edit` hai woh chupchaap us `permissions` array ko "fix" kar sakta hai jise judge karne ko kaha gaya tha. Jo session `bench --site test.localhost console` chala sakta hai uske paas full database access wala IPython shell hai (FRAPPE_FACTS §10). Yeh aisi problems hain jo behtar prompt solve nahi kar sakta aur subagent definition kar sakti hai.

Cost bhi real hai: subagent `fhir.py` aur woh DocType JSON dobara padhta hai jo main session pehle se jaanta hai, aur jo cheez tum uske task message mein daalna bhool gaye (base ref, run id) woh uske paas hoti hi nahi. Isliye practically tum prompt ko agent tabhi banao jab isolation, tool boundary ya repeatable independent opinion us cost ke layak ho.
